WEBVTT

0f3a9c1e-1/12-0
00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:06.920
<v Rohan Mehta>Hi Priya, thanks for jumping on. I know you only have twenty minutes.</v>

0f3a9c1e-1/13-0
00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:09.100
<v Rohan Mehta>So let's keep it focused.</v>

8b21d7aa-2/4-0
00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:18.700
<v Priya Desai>No problem. Quick context: our marketing team approves around three hundred campaign assets a month, and right now it's all email threads.</v>

8b21d7aa-2/5-0
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:27.400
<v Priya Desai>Things get approved by the wrong person, or not at all. Last month we published an ad with an old price.</v>

0f3a9c1e-1/14-0
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.600
<v Rohan Mehta>Ouch. How much budget do you have set aside for fixing this, and when would you want something in place?</v>

8b21d7aa-2/6-0
00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:46.800
<v Priya Desai>We have budget approved for this quarter, around thirty thousand. Ideally live before the January campaign launch.</v>

8b21d7aa-2/7-0
00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:55.900
<v Priya Desai>My concern is adoption. The last tool we bought, half the team never logged in.</v>

0f3a9c1e-1/15-0
00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:08.300
<v Rohan Mehta>That's common. We include onboarding sessions for every team, and approvals can happen straight from Outlook and Teams, so people don't need to learn a new app.</v>

8b21d7aa-2/8-0
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:15.200
<v Priya Desai>Approving from Teams would be huge. Can you send me a short video of that?</v>

0f3a9c1e-1/16-0
00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:24.600
<v Rohan Mehta>Yes, I'll send it today, plus pricing for thirty seats. Could we book a demo with your creative director next week?</v>

8b21d7aa-2/9-0
00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:31.000
<v Priya Desai>Let's do Thursday. I'll loop in Arjun, he runs the creative team.</v>
